SU(2) all-wall payment suffix-weight audit

COMMAND
make -f Makefile.research analyze_su2_aim1_payment_weights
./analyze_su2_aim1_payment_weights 100 2

OUTPUT
DETAIL half_level=2 factor=1 row=0 transform=[0,-2,-2] margin_load=[0,2,2] suffix_weights=[0,2,0]
SU2_AIM1_PAYMENT_WEIGHTS maximum_half_level=100 rows=170425 negative_rows=63750 monotonicity_failures=0 support_failures=0 stable_dominance_failures=0

METHOD
For every half-level K through 100 and every reduced factor q, the
analyzer constructs the finite fusion square F_q=(N_q^(K))^2 and the
margin-coordinate transform T_q=BF_qC.  In each row it puts

  a_s=max(-(T_q)_(r,s),0),
  b_0=a_0,  b_s=a_s-a_(s-1).

It checks that every b_s is nonnegative, that negative rows occur only
for r<2q, and that b is coefficientwise bounded by the stable weights

  2 on r+1<=s<=2q-r-1, and
  1 on 2q-r<=s<=2q+r+1,             when r<q;

  1 on 3r-2q+2<=s<=2q+r+1,          when q<=r<2q.

All checks use exact integer arithmetic.  The zero failures are a
bounded audit of the separate interval-count proof, not an unbounded
proof by computation.

COMPILER FLAGS
g++ -O2 -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wconversion \
  -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror \
  analyze_su2_aim1_payment_weights.cpp \
  -o analyze_su2_aim1_payment_weights

